Rauthy is a lightweight and easy to use Identity Provider supporting OpenID
Connect, OAuth 2, and PAM. It aims to be simple to both set up and operate,
with very secure defaults and lots of config options. It puts heavy emphasis
on Passkeys and strong security in general.

Features include:
- Fully working OIDC / OAuth 2 provider
- PAM logins via custom PAM + NSS modules
- Embedded Hiqlite database (or optional Postgres)
- High-Availability via Raft Consensus
- True passwordless accounts with E-Mail + Magic Link + Passkey
- Dedicated Admin UI and user account dashboard
- OpenID Connect Dynamic Client Registration
- OAuth 2 Device Authorization Grant flow
- Upstream Authentication Providers
- DPoP tokens for decentralized login flows
- SCIM v2 for downstream clients
- Brute-Force and Credential Stuffing detection
- Geolocation-based access restriction
- Prometheus /metrics endpoint
- Hot-Reload TLS certificates
